logog
------------------------------------------
Logog is a portable C++ library to facilitate logging of real-time events in
performance-oriented applications, such as games. It is especially appropriate
for projects that have constrained memory and constrained CPU requirements.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  liblogog-devel-0+git20201022-1bl1
  liblogog0-0+git20201022-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/johnwbyrd/logog

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/johnwbyrd/logog.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack logog-0+git20201022-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./logog-0+git20201022-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/logog-0+git20201022-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/logog-0+git20201022-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/liblogog0-0+git20201022-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/liblogog-devel-0+git20201022-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

